 "result": "Three tests fail for other reasons, going by the subagent's report:\n\n1. **`tests/test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: `asgiref` isn't installed, so `async_to_sync` at `src/tessel/app.py:1096` raises \"Install Tessel with the 'async' extra\". This is a missing optional dependency in the environment, not a source bug.\n\n2. **`tests/test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**: the cause is unknown. It failed in the full run but passed in four isolated reruns, and the subagent couldn't capture its traceback. It expects `ValueError` from `app.open_resource(\"static/index.html\", \"a\")`, and the failure looks order-dependent or flaky.\n\n3. **`tests/test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: strictly this is the same stale Werkzeug, but through a different symptom than the cookie `TypeError`. `Request({}).max_form_memory_size` is `None` instead of `500_000` because Werkzeug 3.0.3 lacks that attribute (added in 3.1). So it's not caused by the `partitioned` cookie problem, though the dependency version is still the underlying reason. The subagent also didn't confirm where Tessel's `Request` reads that value.\n\nOnly tests 1 and 2 are independent of the stale Werkzeug, and only test 2 has no known cause.",
